/* book exam traps: A single slope detector's output is not zero at the carrier: it sits at a bias point on the flank. The balanced slope, Foster-Seeley and ratio detectors give zero at fc. | The S-curve is straight only over a limited range; beyond its peaks (±328 kHz in worked example 2) the output falls again, so more deviation does not give more output. | The Foster-Seeley secondary is tuned to fc, the same as the primary. The 90° comes from the tuned secondary, not from detuning. | The ratio detector limits only slow or moderate amplitude changes. Do not write that it removes all AM. */
